<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arnau Mir de Tost</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1000–<a href="/years/1072">1072</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arnau Mir de Tost was a Catalan frontier lord who led the conquest and resettlement of lands taken from the Muslim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifas</a> in the 11th century. After capturing Àger in 1034 he built a large lordship around it, later the Viscounty of Àger, and founded the canonry of Sant Pere d'Àger. He served the counts of Urgell and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a>, and his daughter's marriage tied him to the counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pallars">Pallars</a> Jussà.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arnau-mir-de-tost.jpg" alt="Arnau Mir de Tost" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Josep Renalias · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sant_Pere_d%27%C3%80ger.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
